! Orig data found in ../data_in/crs/orig_data_2015/crs_ch2o.dat
! Cross-section data for CH2O:
!   CH2O + hv   --> H2 + CO
!               --> H + HCO
! source :  updated to JPL-2011 (JPL_10-6_Final_15June2011.pdf)
! page :    4D-1 (291)
! url :     http://satellite.mpic.de/spectral_atlas/cross_sections/Organics%20%28carbonyls%29/Aldehydes%28aliphatic%29/CH2O_JPL-2010%282011%29_298K_226-375nm%28rec,1nm%29.txt
! Rem1: CRS updated JPL2011
! Rem2: Quantum yield updated JPL2011 given in table 4D4 (p.297)
!   QY(H2+CO) is tdep for wl>330nm. This tdep is not implemented in TUV.
! Rem3: Temperature influence:
!   i) 250-356nm: T dep. according to the formula (see JPL-2011, p.292):
!           crs = crs(wl,298) + GAMMA * (T- 298)
!       where GAMMA is the parameter given below in the last column.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!   ii) GAMMA updated JPL2011
! Rem4: In the ranges [226-249] and [361-373]nm, crs indep of qyield and gamma.
!       Here, for these ranges, qyield and gamma are 0 => these ranges will not
!       contribute to the calculation of the j's table.
!
